# Protocol 14: volcano plot

This notebook ports the thresholding and hit-ranking portion of [DataViz Protocol 14](https://joachimgoedhart.github.io/DataViz-protocols/complete-protocols.html#protocol-14). It uses the exact 3,001-gene table saved by the source workflow from the Becares et al. differential-expression results.

The source defines an increased hit as `log2_FoldChange > 1.5` and `minus_log10_pvalue > 5`, a decreased hit as `log2_FoldChange < -1.5` and `minus_log10_pvalue > 5`, and everything else as unchanged.

```biolang
let genes = read_csv("data/protocol_14.csv")
let increased = genes |> filter(|row| row.log2_FoldChange > 1.5 && row.minus_log10_pvalue > 5)
let decreased = genes |> filter(|row| row.log2_FoldChange < -1.5 && row.minus_log10_pvalue > 5)
let unchanged = genes |> filter(|row| !(row.log2_FoldChange > 1.5 && row.minus_log10_pvalue > 5) && !(row.log2_FoldChange < -1.5 && row.minus_log10_pvalue > 5))
{
    genes: nrow(genes),
    increased: nrow(increased),
    decreased: nrow(decreased),
    unchanged: nrow(unchanged)
}
```

The published workflow ranks only increased and decreased genes by Manhattan distance from the origin: `minus_log10_pvalue + abs(log2_FoldChange)`.

```biolang
let hits = genes
    |> filter(|row| row.Change != "Unchanged")
    |> mutate("distance", |row| row.minus_log10_pvalue + abs(row.log2_FoldChange))
    |> arrange("-distance")
let top_ten = hits |> head(10)
top_ten
```

## Exact published output

![DataViz Protocol 14: volcano plot](figures/source/Protocol_14.png)

This is the source repository's `Protocol_14.png`, copied byte for byte. The displayed thresholds, labels, colours, annotations and layout are the canonical source output, not a substitute.

```biolang
assert nrow(genes) == 3001, "exact source gene rows"
assert nrow(increased) == 8, "exact increased count"
assert nrow(decreased) == 12, "exact decreased count"
assert nrow(unchanged) == 2981, "exact unchanged count"
assert top_ten[0].Gene == "Osbpl3", "source top-ranked hit"
assert top_ten[1].Gene == "Spp1", "source second-ranked hit"
assert top_ten[9].Gene == "Lrtm2", "source tenth-ranked hit"
"Exact thresholds, hit ranking, source table, and canonical PNG verified."
```

